V(OHSM, IO_A,
  "A 66-year-old woman with a body mass index of 42 kg/m2 has obesity hypoventilation syndrome, confirmed by exclusion. Her husband has witnessed few apneas, and polysomnography with continuous carbon dioxide monitoring shows sleep-related hypoventilation. Which first-line treatment fits her?",
  [["Weight loss plus bilevel positive airway pressure",
    "Correct. First-line therapy for obesity hypoventilation syndrome is a weight loss program with positive airway pressure, and the device follows the overlap: with sleep-related hypoventilation it is bilevel positive airway pressure. Her few witnessed apneas, older age and female sex fit that 10% subgroup."],
   ["Weight loss plus continuous positive airway pressure",
    "Continuous positive airway pressure is the first-line device when obesity hypoventilation coexists with obstructive sleep apnea. Tell: her study shows sleep-related hypoventilation with few witnessed apneas, which calls for bilevel pressure.", "competing diagnosis"],
   ["Tracheostomy with nocturnal ventilation",
    "Tracheostomy with nocturnal ventilation is very effective, but it is second line, for patients who fail or do not tolerate first-line therapy. Tell: she is just starting treatment and has failed nothing.", "wrong stage or severity"],
   ["Bariatric surgery as first therapy",
    "Bariatric surgery for weight loss may be helpful, but it sits in second line, after first-line therapy fails or is not tolerated. Tell: first line is a weight loss program plus positive airway pressure.", "wrong stage or severity"]],
  CS(33, 30, 32), "first-line", "treatment"),

